  "r3": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "7. The Creator has created a certain and effective disguise",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "for ignorance which can be readily commanded, viz. silence,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "which, especially in an assembly of learned men, becomes to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "ignorant folks a befitting ornament.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r4": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "8. When I knew a little, I was blinded by pride, as",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "an elephant is by rut; and my mind was elated with the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "thought “I am an omniscient being”. When ( however ),",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "by keeping company with the wise, I learnt bit by bit, the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "fever of pride entirely disappeared at the thought that",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "I was a fool.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r5": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "9. When munching with unparalleled relish and delight",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "a human bone, fleshless, stinking, covered with a swarm",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "of worms, clammed with saliva, and nauseating, a cur is not",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "abashed to behold even Indra standing near: a mean wretch",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "does not mind the worthlessness of his belongings.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r6": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "10. The Ganges falls from heaven on the head of S'iva;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "from the head of the Lord of beings to the mountain",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "Himâlaya; from that lofty mountain to the plain ( lit. the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "earth ); and from thence into the ocean. Thus going down",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "and down the Ganges here has been reduced to a low posi-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "sion: or there is no cause for wonder; in a hundred ways",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "ruin overtakes those that have lost their discernment.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r7": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "11. It is possible to counteract (the working of) fire with",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "water, and the heat of the sun with an umbrella; to control",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "a lordly elephant with a sharp goad, and an infuriated bull",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "and an ass with a cudgel; to cure illness by taking medi-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "cine, and to countermine the ( effect of ) poison by the use",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "of spells. Every thing has an antidote prescribed for it in the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "S'astras, but for a fool there is none.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
